@meta
id: 16-15
title: Drill — split, edit, close
chapter: 16
type: drill
skills: split-window, window-nav
par: 75
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: open the file, edit, close the tab, back to the first one
open: customer.provider.ts

@brief
Eight times: `errors.json` says `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` is a `400`; make
it `404`. The provider throws `CUSTOMER_MISSING`; make it
`CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND`. The errors file is not open.

The shape to drill: split it open above, fix it, `:wq` to write it and
close its window in one go, and you are back in the provider with a
single window. Fix that, `:wq` again, and that one ends vim.

@keys
| `:sp errors.json` | open it above |
| `:wq` | write this buffer and close this window |
| `Ctrl-W c` | close the window without writing, if there was nothing to write |

@hints
`:sp errors.json`, `/CUSTOMER`, `f4`, `cw404`, `Esc`, `:wq`. Then
`/MISSING`, `cw`, `NOT_FOUND`, `Esc`, `:wq`.
--
Two `:wq` with different meanings: the first closes a window, the
second closes vim. Feel the difference; it is the one that catches
people out in 16-13.

@solution
    :sp errors.json<Enter>  /CUSTOMER<Enter>  f4  cw 404 <Esc>  :wq<Enter>
    /MISSING<Enter>  cw NOT_FOUND <Esc>  :wq<Enter>

Sixty-odd keystrokes. The split costs the filename and nothing else;
closing it costs nothing at all because you were writing anyway.

This is the reference-file pattern in its smallest form: open beside,
take what you need, close, carry on. It generalises to `:vs` when the
lines are long and to `Ctrl-W o` when you opened more than one.

@start customer.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { CustomerRepository } from './customer.repository';

@injectable()
export class CustomerProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(CustomerRepository) protected customerRepository: CustomerRepository,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const customer = await this.customerRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!customer) {
      throw exception('CUSTOMER_MISSING');
    }

    return customer;
  }
}

@expected customer.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { CustomerRepository } from './customer.repository';

@injectable()
export class CustomerProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(CustomerRepository) protected customerRepository: CustomerRepository,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const customer = await this.customerRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!customer) {
      throw exception('CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return customer;
  }
}

@start errors.json
{
  "ORDER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 400, "sentry": false },
  "REFUND_FAILED": { "statusCode": 502, "sentry": true }
}

@expected errors.json
{
  "ORDER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "REFUND_FAILED": { "statusCode": 502, "sentry": true }
}
